# gen3_2f85 mesh content manifest.
#
# SHA-256 of every one of the 26 unique mesh files referenced by the
# gen3_2f85 URDF after the wrist-camera subtree is removed (34 <mesh>
# references resolve to 26 unique files, since several links reuse the same
# mesh for visual and collision geometry).
#
# Each hash was computed twice and cross-checked:
#   1. from the actual installed package copy used by the already-validated
#      robot-module equivalence test (kortex_description meshes from a
#      local ros2_kortex 0.2.6 build; robotiq_description meshes from the
#      apt-installed ros-jazzy-robotiq-description 0.0.1 package);
#   2. independently, by fetching the same package-relative file fresh from
#      the official upstream Git tag (Kinovarobotics/ros2_kortex tag 0.2.6
#      for kortex_description/..., PicknikRobotics/ros2_robotiq_gripper tag
#      0.0.1 for robotiq_description/...).
# All 26 files matched exactly between the two independently obtained
# copies.
#
# Format: <sha256>  <package>/<package-relative-path>
# scripts/setup_gen3_2f85_module.py verifies every mesh referenced by the
# upstream URDF against this exact manifest -- path set and hash -- before
# rewriting any URI. It fails on a missing file, an unrecognized/extra mesh
# reference not in this manifest, or a hash mismatch.
